  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first of the 6 allowed runs (\"5 witnesses, 4 names, composes nothing\").\n\n**Rule** (`LVMC_11_43_010_A.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** `x` is a vehicle (member of the `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle` aggregate).\n- **When it applies:** `x` occupies some roundabout region.\n- **The duty:** for every roundabout region `r` that `x` occupies, `x` is not moving clockwise about `r`. This uses `drv_motion_clockwise_about_region(x, r)` with `p.speed_resolution` and `p.circulation_sine_tolerance`, in that order.\n- **Choices:** I added no narrowings. The node's own reading of \"counterclockwise\" (no clockwise motion; standing still or moving straight toward or away from the centre complies) is already on record, so I didn't repeat it.\n- I left the harness's `zeroMetres` helper in place; it isn't used.\n\n**Witnesses:** the roundabout is a 60 m square centred on the origin, and the car moves at 10 m/s, 15 m from the centre.\n\n| Scenario | Scene | Expected |\n|---|---|---|\n| `forbid` | Car drives clockwise round the island | violated |\n| `permit` | Car drives counter-clockwise round the island | compliant |\n| `idle` | Car is on an ordinary road block far from the roundabout | not applicable |\n| `blind` | Same scene as `forbid`, with velocity masked | unknown |\n| `branch_1` | Car on an entry approach drives straight toward the centre at 5 m/s | compliant |\n\nBefore the gate I ran one stray no-op shell command (`true`); it did nothing and didn't use a gate run. `task_result.md` mentions it and is in the working directory.",
